00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:34.267
Alright,

00:07:34.267 --> 00:07:36.100
a number analogy!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.900
One makes four,

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:39.733
two makes six,

00:07:39.733 --> 00:07:41.533
three makes eight,

00:07:41.533 --> 00:07:43.367
so four makes...

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:43.967
what?

00:07:43.967 --> 00:07:44.567
A.

00:07:44.567 --> 00:07:45.167
Nine,

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:45.767
B.

00:07:45.767 --> 00:07:46.400
Ten,

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.000
C.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:47.600
Eleven,

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:48.800
or D.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:49.400
Twelve?

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.633
Five seconds!

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.600
TIME'S UP!

00:07:58.267 --> 00:07:58.733
It's...

00:07:58.733 --> 00:07:59.200
B,

00:07:59.200 --> 00:07:59.667
ten!

00:07:59.667 --> 00:08:02.500
Each number is doubled then add

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:02.967
two:

00:08:02.967 --> 00:08:05.333
